The thing that always gets me is the way you're able to function just
as well when you have *one* hit point as when you have a hundred. I
mean, if you're one hit point away from dying...shouldn't you be
staggering around or collapsing on the dungeon floor, slipping in the
blood gushing out from your wounds, gasping for air, blinded by agony,
fainting from loss of blood... well, okay, maybe a little graphic, but
you get the point! How is it that you can perform a difficult task -
i.e. shooting an arrow accurately or casting a spell -- just as easily
as you can when at your HP maximum?

Also, apart from a very few special attacks (i.e. poison, decapitation
etc) you're never permanently handicapped by any fighting. In real
life, sooner or later an enemy arrow would take out your eye and you'd
be blinded for the rest of the game. Or you'd lose an arm or a leg.
But in Nethack, somehow these essential body parts are magically
regenerated (or invulnerable.) Not very logical...

